{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And you shall make its dishes… and its flat pans.</b> He sealed all the implements of the table with the מְנַקִּיּוֹת to indicate that a person will be sustained in purity, not from theft; and so he shall give from his table to the poor in a clean manner, not by way of humiliation. And it is written: ״וְנָתַתָּ עַל הַשֻּׁלְחָן לֶחֶם פָּנִים לְפָנַי תָּמִיד״ (Exodus 25:30) — for from heaven HaShem, blessed be He, gives him his bread with shining faces, and his bread will not be lacking. This is what it says: 'לְפָנַי תָּמִיד' — for the bread that a person asks as is fitting is given to him with shining faces and forever, as we explained in the portion of וַיְחִי on the verse ״בַּבֹּקֶר יֹאכַל עַד״ (Genesis 49:27). And there were twelve loaves, six loaves of each arrangement, corresponding to the twelve zodiacal signs, of which six serve by day and six by night — for through them the influx comes to the world from the First Cause, blessed be He. And all that a person asks as is fitting is given to him with shining faces, by means of the signs that serve by day; and what he asks not as is fitting is given to him with darkened faces, by means of the signs that serve by night. And so with the bread of Aaron, which he merited from the table on high — the breast, which has twelve ribs, six on the right and six on the left; and it is fitting to attribute the right to shining faces and the left to darkened faces. And this is what it says: 'לֶחֶם פָּנִים לְפָנַי תָּמִיד' — just as the bread turns its faces toward Me, so I toward it — whether shining or whether darkened. All these are my words by way of allusion, because I saw that most of the commentators who approach to explain the plain sense of Scripture, and whose way is not to speak of matters of allusion — nevertheless, in this portion they made allusions, each according to his understanding. Therefore my heart moved me also to make allusions, to say: perhaps the blind ones in the camp of the Hebrews will hear and take instruction."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:23:18.612636271Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}